workedExamples.solution_text:
(a) The total area is $1$. Symmetry divides it equally at the mean.

$\begin{aligned} &\mathrel{\phantom{=}}P(X>48)\\ &=\frac{1}{2}\times1\\ &=0.5 \end{aligned}$

(b) Since $43$ and $53$ are equally distant from $48$, the area between $48$ and $53$ is also approximately $0.34$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\definecolor{regionfill}{HTML}{DCEBE0}
\fill[regionfill] (1,0)--plot[domain=1:3.6,samples=70,smooth,variable=\x] ({\x},{2.4*exp(-\x*\x/2)})--(3.6,0)--cycle;
\draw[thick] plot[domain=-3.6:3.6,samples=120,smooth,variable=\x] ({\x},{2.4*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[->] (-3.9,0)--(4.1,0) node[right] {$x$};
\foreach \a/\b in {-1/43,0/48,1/53} {\draw[dashed] (\a,0)--(\a,{2.4*exp(-\a*\a/2)});\draw (\a,0)--(\a,-0.12) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\b$};}
\path (-0.5,0.7) node {$0.34$};
\path (0.5,0.7) node {$0.34$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\begin{aligned} &\mathrel{\phantom{=}}P(X>53)\\ &\approx0.5-0.34\\ &=0.16 \end{aligned}$

